WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
Data pipelines break silently.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:08.500
A column gets renamed upstream, a sync goes stale —

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.500
and your dashboards are wrong before anyone notices.

4
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:18.500
DQ Sentinel is an autonomous data-quality agent that watches Fivetran pipelines,

5
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.000
inspects the data in BigQuery, and diagnoses the root cause with Gemini —

6
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.500
but it never writes anything without a human's say-so.

7
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.000
It's a seven-step loop, not a chatbot:

8
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.500
scan, detect, inspect, diagnose, approve, act, verify.

9
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:41.000
Gemini does the diagnosis; the Fivetran MCP server is the only way it touches pipelines.

10
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.500
The approval gate is structural — the model has no write tool until a human approves.

11
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.500
Here's the agent, running on Cloud Run.

12
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.000
I pick the transactions connection and hit Run scan now.

13
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.500
It scans Fivetran and runs data-quality checks in BigQuery against a rolling baseline,

14
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:06.000
and flags a freshness violation: this table's data is over three days stale.

15
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.500
Now it pauses.

16
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:16.000
Gemini diagnoses the cause: the connection is healthy, but a normal sync never refreshed the data.

17
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.500
It proposes a fix — a full re-sync.

18
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:27.000
Crucially, it shows me the exact Fivetran tool call it wants to run, with its arguments.

19
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.500
I can approve, reject, or edit the targets. Nothing is written until I click.

20
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.000
I'll approve.

21
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Now — and only now — the agent executes the write through Fivetran's MCP server.

22
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Then it verifies: it polls until the sync completes and re-runs the exact check that failed.

23
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.500
Freshness went from 4,541 minutes stale to zero.

24
00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:59.000
Status: resolved.

25
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:06.000
And it splits time-to-resolution into agent time versus the sync wait — so the human time is honest.

26
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Every run produces an incident report: what broke, the root cause, the action, and before-and-after metrics.

27
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:19.500
The approval gate means an autonomous agent you can actually trust with production pipelines.

28
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.500
Built on Gemini, Fivetran MCP, BigQuery, and Cloud Run.

29
00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:28.000
Thanks for watching.
